    "problem_statement": "ZMS mount operations always auto-format erased flash when no valid header is found. There is no way to prevent auto-formatting and instead get an error (ENOTSUP) when mounting an erased partition. Add a mount_flags field to the zms_fs structure and a ZMS_MOUNT_FLAG_NO_FORMAT flag so that zms_mount() returns -ENOTSUP instead of formatting when the flag is set, while preserving the default auto-format behaviour when mount_flags is 0.",
